{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790258963,"nonce":"LPpEqFnmLF/PGV+BfnoTegCHij4=","title":"LLVM: promoting zb_call_1 fails with \"Expected function type for indirect call, got: I64\"","message":"With ZYPY_LLVM=1 and ZYNTAX_OSR_TRACE=1, the program below sometimes promotes the library's `zb_call_1` (`[osr] promote HirId(490): context=true closure=4`), and that LLVM compile fails with `Code generation error: Expected function type for indirect call, got: I64`; the function stays on Cranelift, so the output is right. Seen on main dea6d08b (1 of 20 runs promote it) and more often on the s5 start-up branch (15 of 20), where the promotion timing differs. The failure is deterministic once the promotion is attempted: an indirect call whose callee value is typed I64 reaches the LLVM lowering without a function type.\n\n    def mk(k):\n        return lambda x: x * k + 1\n    fs = [mk(i) for i in range(20)]\n    total = 0\n    for r in range(200000):\n        total += fs[r % 20](r)\n    print(total)\n    class V:\n        def __init__(self, x, y):\n            self.x = x\n            self.y = y\n        def __add__(self, o):\n            return V(self.x + o.x, self.y + o.y)\n    acc = V(0, 0)\n    for i in range(100000):\n        acc = acc + V(i % 3, i % 5)\n    print(acc.x, acc.y)\n    nums = sorted(range(5000), key=lambda v: (v * 7919) % 10007, reverse=True)\n    print(nums[0])\n\nRelated closed issue: 6de111f (an indirect call through a function address held as an integer panicked).","files":null}]}